# Starter egress allowlist: the hosts opencode needs. Copy it to
# ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/csb/allowed-hosts.opencode, where csb reads it
# under --filter-egress for agent=opencode.
#
# csb prefers allowed-hosts.<agent> and falls back to a plain allowed-hosts, so
# an unsuffixed file stays the shared list for every agent that has none of its
# own.
#
# Format: one host per line; `#` comments and blank lines ignored. A leading
# `*.` matches subdomains only, so list a bare parent domain separately when it
# is also wanted.
#
# These entries are add-only: they union with --allow-host and any config
# layer's allow_host=. The file is read once per launch, so an edit applies to
# the next one.
#
# Which hosts opencode reaches is decided by the PROVIDER, not by opencode:
# every provider in its catalog is enabled by its own API-key variable, and
# `token_env=` names which one a launch carries.
#
# So keep this file to what you ALWAYS reach -- the provider matching the
# adapter's default of OPENROUTER_API_KEY is below -- and let a PROFILE carry
# any other. One profile per (agent, provider) pair keeps each launch's
# allowlist as small as that launch needs, which listing every provider you
# have ever used here would not:
#
#   # ~/.config/csb/profiles/oc-anthropic
#   agent=opencode
#   token_env=ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   token_cmd=op read op://vault/anthropic/key
#   allow_host=api.anthropic.com
#
# csb has no provider axis of its own yet; docs/PLAN-010-agents.md section 12
# records what one would look like and what would trigger building it.

# --- the always-reached provider ---------------------------------------------
openrouter.ai

# Deliberately NOT listed. Each was measured: a full tool-using turn against
# OpenRouter, under --filter-egress with openrouter.ai as the only allowed
# host, produced TWO connections and no denials at all (2026-09-18, opencode
# 1.18.30). Nothing below was attempted, because the companion env keeps it
# from being attempted -- the agent adapter injects both as its lowest setenv
# layer, so this file and those knobs are already in sync:
#
#   OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE=1     the update check
#   OPENCODE_DISABLE_MODELS_FETCH=1   the models.dev catalog refresh; the
#                                     binary carries a build-time snapshot,
#                                     which is what the model picker lists
#
#   models.dev            model catalog (OPENCODE_MODELS_URL overrides it)
#   opncd.ai              session sharing; config "share": "disabled" also
#                         turns it off, and nothing shares by default
#   registry.npmjs.org    runtime SDK install, reached only by an exotic
#                         provider; every mainstream one is compiled in
#
# Telemetry needs no entry: it is OTLP-only and inert unless
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT is set, which the env scrub does not carry in.
